module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Finprod
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Smooth.Basic
public import TauCeti.Data.ZMod.MonoidHomEquiv

/-!
# Smoothness of fixed-point quotients under tame group actions

Let `R` be a commutative semiring, `A` a commutative `R`-algebra, and `Γ` a monoid acting on `A` by
`R`-algebra automorphisms `ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)`. On `Spec A`, the closed subscheme of `Γ`-fixed
points is represented by the coinvariant quotient `A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ`, where
`fixedPointIdeal ρ` is the ideal generated by all displacements `ρ γ a - a` (`fixedPointIdeal_def`,
`sub_mem_fixedPointIdeal`, `fixedPointIdeal_le_iff`, `fixedPointIdeal_eq_span`). The quotient map
equalizes every `ρ γ` with the identity (`mk_fixedPointIdeal_apply`, `mkₐ_fixedPointIdeal_comp`),
so homomorphisms out of `A` vanish on `fixedPointIdeal ρ` if and only if they are `Γ`-invariant
(`fixedPointIdeal_le_ker_iff`, `fixedPointIdeal_le_algHom_ker_iff`), giving the universal property
`fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv` (`fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv_apply`,
`fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv_symm_apply_mk`). A trivial action cuts out the zero ideal
(`fixedPointIdeal_eq_bot_iff`, `fixedPointIdeal_one`, `fixedPointQuotientOneAlgEquiv`,
`fixedPointQuotientOneAlgEquiv_mk`), and for a group generated by a single element `g₀` the
displacements of `g₀` alone span `fixedPointIdeal ρ` (`fixedPointIdeal_eq_span_of_mem_zpowers`).

When `Γ` is finite and `A` is of finite type over `R`, the twisted Leibniz identity
`ρ γ (a * b) - a * b = (ρ γ a - a) * ρ γ b + a * (ρ γ b - b)` shows that displacements of a finite
algebra generating set generate `fixedPointIdeal ρ` (`fg_fixedPointIdeal`), so finite presentation
descends to the quotient (`finitePresentation_quotient_fixedPointIdeal`).

When `Γ` is a group whose order `Nat.card Γ` is a unit in `R` (so either `Γ` is finite or `R` is
trivial) and `A` is formally smooth over `R`, the quotient `A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ` is formally
smooth over `R` (`formallySmooth_quotient_fixedPointIdeal`), and therefore smooth when `A` is smooth
(`smooth_quotient_fixedPointIdeal`). Given a square-zero ideal `I` of `B` and a `Γ`-invariant map
`g : A →ₐ[R] B ⧸ I`, any lift `f₀ : A →ₐ[R] B` of `g` can be averaged over `Γ` to produce a
`Γ`-invariant `R`-algebra lift (`exists_invariant_lift_of_sq_eq_bot`).

Similarly, when `Γ` acts on a commutative `R`-algebra `B` with `IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R)`,
`algebraMap R B` injective, and `B^Γ ⊆ Set.range (algebraMap R B)`, Reynolds averaging yields an
`R`-linear retraction `linearRetractOfIsUnitCard` of `algebraMap R B`
(`algebraMap_linearRetractOfIsUnitCard`, `linearRetractOfIsUnitCard_algebraMap`) that identifies
`(B ⊗[R] T)^Γ` with `T` (`includeRight_lid_rTensor_linearRetractOfIsUnitCard_of_fixed`).

Finally, the order-two action `tensorSwapAction R A` (`tensorSwapAction_ofAdd_one`) exchanging the
two factors of `A ⊗[R] A` cuts out the kernel of multiplication `A ⊗[R] A →ₐ[R] A`
(`fixedPointIdeal_tensorSwapAction`), identifying the fixed-point quotient with `A`
(`quotientFixedPointIdealTensorSwapAlgEquiv`, `quotientFixedPointIdealTensorSwapAlgEquiv_mk_tmul`).

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointIdeal`: the ideal of `A` generated by all displacements `ρ γ a - a`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv`: `R`-algebra homomorphisms out of
  `A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ` correspond bijectively to `Γ`-invariant homomorphisms out of `A`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointQuotientOneAlgEquiv`: for the trivial action, `A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal 1`
  is canonically isomorphic to `A`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.linearRetractOfIsUnitCard`: Reynolds-averaging `R`-linear retraction
  `B →ₗ[R] R` of `algebraMap R B` when `IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R)`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.tensorSwapAction` and
  `TauCeti.Algebra.quotientFixedPointIdealTensorSwapAlgEquiv`: the `ℤ/2ℤ`-action swapping the
  factors of `A ⊗[R] A` and the isomorphism of its fixed-point quotient with `A`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointIdeal_def`, `TauCeti.Algebra.sub_mem_fixedPointIdeal`,
  `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointIdeal_le_iff`, `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointIdeal_eq_span`,
  `TauCeti.Algebra.mk_fixedPointIdeal_apply`, `TauCeti.Algebra.mkₐ_fixedPointIdeal_comp`,
  `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointIdeal_le_ker_iff`, `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointIdeal_le_algHom_ker_iff`,
  `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv_apply`,
  `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv_symm_apply_mk`,
  `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointIdeal_eq_bot_iff`, `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointIdeal_one`,
  `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointQuotientOneAlgEquiv_mk`, and
  `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointIdeal_eq_span_of_mem_zpowers`: characteristic API for
  `fixedPointIdeal` and its quotient.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.fg_fixedPointIdeal` and
  `TauCeti.Algebra.finitePresentation_quotient_fixedPointIdeal`: finite generation of the
  displacement ideal and finite presentation of the fixed-point quotient for finite `Γ`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.exists_invariant_lift_of_sq_eq_bot`,
  `TauCeti.Algebra.formallySmooth_quotient_fixedPointIdeal`, and
  `TauCeti.Algebra.smooth_quotient_fixedPointIdeal`: invariant lifting across square-zero extensions
  and Edixhoven's tame fixed-point smoothness theorem.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.algebraMap_linearRetractOfIsUnitCard`,
  `TauCeti.Algebra.linearRetractOfIsUnitCard_algebraMap`, and
  `TauCeti.Algebra.includeRight_lid_rTensor_linearRetractOfIsUnitCard_of_fixed`: specification of
  the Reynolds retraction and identification of `(B ⊗[R] T)^Γ` with `T`.
* `TauCeti.Algebra.tensorSwapAction_ofAdd_one`,
  `TauCeti.Algebra.fixedPointIdeal_tensorSwapAction`, and
  `TauCeti.Algebra.quotientFixedPointIdealTensorSwapAlgEquiv_mk_tmul`: the displacement ideal of the
  factor-swap action on `A ⊗[R] A` equals the kernel of multiplication `A ⊗[R] A →ₐ[R] A`.

## References

* B. Edixhoven, *Néron models and tame ramification*, Compositio Math. 81 (1992), Prop. 3.1
  (p. 293) and Prop. 3.4 (pp. 294–295).
-/

public noncomputable section

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace TauCeti.Algebra

section Ideal

variable {R A Γ : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] [Monoid Γ]

/-- The **fixed-point (coinvariant) ideal** of an action `ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)` of a monoid `Γ` on
a commutative `R`-algebra `A`, generated by all displacements `ρ γ a - a`. On affine schemes, its
quotient `A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ` represents the closed subfunctor of `Γ`-fixed points. -/
def fixedPointIdeal (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) : Ideal A :=
  ⨆ γ : Γ, Ideal.span (Set.range fun a : A ↦ ρ γ a - a)

/-- `fixedPointIdeal ρ` is the supremum over `γ : Γ` of the ideals spanned by `a ↦ ρ γ a - a`. -/
theorem fixedPointIdeal_def (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) :
    fixedPointIdeal ρ = ⨆ γ : Γ, Ideal.span (Set.range fun a : A ↦ ρ γ a - a) :=
  (rfl)

/-- Every displacement `ρ γ a - a` belongs to `fixedPointIdeal ρ`. -/
theorem sub_mem_fixedPointIdeal (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) (γ : Γ) (a : A) :
    ρ γ a - a ∈ fixedPointIdeal ρ :=
  Ideal.mem_iSup_of_mem γ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨a, rfl⟩)

/-- `fixedPointIdeal ρ` is contained in an ideal `J` if and only if `J` contains all displacements
`ρ γ a - a`. -/
theorem fixedPointIdeal_le_iff {ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)} {J : Ideal A} :
    fixedPointIdeal ρ ≤ J ↔ ∀ (γ : Γ) (a : A), ρ γ a - a ∈ J := by
  rw [fixedPointIdeal_def, iSup_le_iff]
  refine forall_congr' fun γ ↦ ?_
  rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.range_subset_iff]
  rfl

/-- `fixedPointIdeal ρ` is spanned by the set of all displacements `ρ γ a - a`. -/
theorem fixedPointIdeal_eq_span (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) :
    fixedPointIdeal ρ = Ideal.span {x : A | ∃ (γ : Γ) (a : A), ρ γ a - a = x} := by
  refine le_antisymm (fixedPointIdeal_le_iff.2 fun γ a ↦ Ideal.subset_span ⟨γ, a, rfl⟩) ?_
  rw [Ideal.span_le]
  rintro _ ⟨γ, a, rfl⟩
  exact sub_mem_fixedPointIdeal ρ γ a

/-- The quotient map `A →+* A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ` identifies `ρ γ a` with `a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mk_fixedPointIdeal_apply (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) (γ : Γ) (a : A) :
    Ideal.Quotient.mk (fixedPointIdeal ρ) (ρ γ a) = Ideal.Quotient.mk (fixedPointIdeal ρ) a :=
  Ideal.Quotient.eq.2 (sub_mem_fixedPointIdeal ρ γ a)

/-- Precomposing the quotient algebra map `A →ₐ[R] A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ` with `ρ γ` leaves it
unchanged. -/
@[simp]
theorem mkₐ_fixedPointIdeal_comp (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) (γ : Γ) :
    (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R (fixedPointIdeal ρ)).comp (ρ γ : A →ₐ[R] A) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R (fixedPointIdeal ρ) := by
  ext a
  exact mk_fixedPointIdeal_apply ρ γ a

/-- A ring homomorphism out of `A` vanishes on `fixedPointIdeal ρ` if and only if it is
`Γ`-invariant on elements. -/
theorem fixedPointIdeal_le_ker_iff {S : Type*} [Semiring S] (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) (φ : A →+* S) :
    fixedPointIdeal ρ ≤ RingHom.ker φ ↔ ∀ (γ : Γ) (a : A), φ (ρ γ a) = φ a := by
  rw [fixedPointIdeal_le_iff]
  refine forall_congr' fun γ ↦ forall_congr' fun a ↦ ?_
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker]
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  · calc φ (ρ γ a) = φ (ρ γ a - a + a) := by rw [sub_add_cancel]
      _ = φ (ρ γ a - a) + φ a := map_add φ _ _
      _ = φ a := by rw [h, zero_add]
  · calc φ (ρ γ a - a) = φ (ρ γ a) + φ (-a) := by rw [sub_eq_add_neg, map_add]
      _ = φ a + φ (-a) := by rw [h]
      _ = 0 := by rw [← map_add, add_neg_cancel, map_zero]

/-- An `R`-algebra homomorphism `g : A →ₐ[R] B` vanishes on `fixedPointIdeal ρ` if and only if
`g ∘ ρ γ = g` for every `γ : Γ`. -/
theorem fixedPointIdeal_le_algHom_ker_iff {B : Type*} [Semiring B] [Algebra R B]
    (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) (g : A →ₐ[R] B) :
    fixedPointIdeal ρ ≤ RingHom.ker g.toRingHom ↔
      ∀ γ : Γ, g.comp (ρ γ : A →ₐ[R] A) = g := by
  rw [fixedPointIdeal_le_ker_iff]
  refine forall_congr' fun γ ↦ ?_
  simp only [AlgHom.ext_iff, AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgEquiv.coe_toAlgHom, AlgHom.toRingHom_eq_coe,
    RingHom.coe_coe]

/-- **Universal property of the fixed-point quotient.** `R`-algebra homomorphisms
`(A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ) →ₐ[R] B` correspond bijectively to `Γ`-invariant `R`-algebra homomorphisms
`A →ₐ[R] B`. -/
def fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) (B : Type*) [Semiring B] [Algebra R B] :
    ((A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ) →ₐ[R] B) ≃
      {g : A →ₐ[R] B // ∀ γ : Γ, g.comp (ρ γ : A →ₐ[R] A) = g} where
  toFun f := ⟨f.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R (fixedPointIdeal ρ)), fun γ ↦ by
    rw [AlgHom.comp_assoc, mkₐ_fixedPointIdeal_comp]⟩
  invFun g := Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ (fixedPointIdeal ρ) g.1 fun a ha ↦
    RingHom.mem_ker.1 (((fixedPointIdeal_le_algHom_ker_iff ρ g.1).2 g.2) ha)
  left_inv f := Ideal.Quotient.algHom_ext _ (AlgHom.ext fun _ ↦ rfl)
  right_inv g := Subtype.ext (AlgHom.ext fun _ ↦ rfl)

/-- The `Γ`-invariant homomorphism attached to `f : (A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ) →ₐ[R] B` is
`f ∘ mkₐ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv_apply {B : Type*} [Semiring B] [Algebra R B]
    (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) (f : (A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ) →ₐ[R] B) :
    (fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv ρ B f).1 =
      f.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R (fixedPointIdeal ρ)) :=
  (rfl)

/-- Evaluating the descended homomorphism `(fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv ρ B).symm g` on the
quotient class of `a` recovers `g a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv_symm_apply_mk {B : Type*} [Semiring B] [Algebra R B]
    (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) (g : {g : A →ₐ[R] B // ∀ γ : Γ, g.comp (ρ γ : A →ₐ[R] A) = g})
    (a : A) :
    (fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv ρ B).symm g (Ideal.Quotient.mk (fixedPointIdeal ρ) a) =
      g.1 a :=
  (rfl)

/-- `fixedPointIdeal ρ` vanishes if and only if the action `ρ` is trivial. -/
@[simp]
theorem fixedPointIdeal_eq_bot_iff (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) :
    fixedPointIdeal ρ = ⊥ ↔ ρ = 1 := by
  rw [eq_bot_iff, fixedPointIdeal_le_iff]
  simp only [Ideal.mem_bot, sub_eq_zero, DFunLike.ext_iff, MonoidHom.one_apply, AlgEquiv.one_apply]

/-- The trivial action cuts out the zero ideal. -/
@[simp]
theorem fixedPointIdeal_one : fixedPointIdeal (1 : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) = ⊥ :=
  (fixedPointIdeal_eq_bot_iff _).2 rfl

/-- For the trivial action, the fixed-point quotient `A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal 1` is canonically
isomorphic to `A`. -/
def fixedPointQuotientOneAlgEquiv :
    (A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal (1 : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A))) ≃ₐ[R] A :=
  (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq R fixedPointIdeal_one).trans (AlgEquiv.quotientBot R A)

/-- `fixedPointQuotientOneAlgEquiv` sends the quotient class of `a` to `a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem fixedPointQuotientOneAlgEquiv_mk (a : A) :
    fixedPointQuotientOneAlgEquiv (R := R) (Γ := Γ)
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (fixedPointIdeal (1 : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A))) a) = a :=
  (rfl)

end Ideal

section Cyclic

variable {R A G : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] [Group G]

/-- If `G` is generated as a group by a single element `g₀`, then `fixedPointIdeal ρ` is spanned
by the displacements `ρ g₀ a - a` of `g₀` alone. -/
theorem fixedPointIdeal_eq_span_of_mem_zpowers (ρ : G →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) (g₀ : G)
    (hg₀ : ∀ g : G, g ∈ Subgroup.zpowers g₀) :
    fixedPointIdeal ρ = Ideal.span (Set.range fun a : A ↦ ρ g₀ a - a) := by
  let J := Ideal.span (Set.range fun a : A ↦ ρ g₀ a - a)
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (Ideal.span_le.2 <| Set.range_subset_iff.2 (sub_mem_fixedPointIdeal ρ g₀))
  -- The elements of `G` whose displacements lie in `J` form a subgroup containing `g₀`.
  let H : Subgroup G :=
    { carrier := {g : G | ∀ a : A, ρ g a - a ∈ J}
      mul_mem' {g₁ g₂} h₁ h₂ a := by
        have hcocycle : ρ (g₁ * g₂) a - a = (ρ g₁ (ρ g₂ a) - ρ g₂ a) + (ρ g₂ a - a) := by
          rw [map_mul, AlgEquiv.mul_apply]
          ring
        rw [hcocycle]
        exact add_mem (h₁ (ρ g₂ a)) (h₂ a)
      one_mem' a := by simp
      inv_mem' {g} hg a := by
        have hinv : ρ g⁻¹ a - a = -(ρ g (ρ g⁻¹ a) - ρ g⁻¹ a) := by
          have hcancel : ρ g (ρ g⁻¹ a) = a := by
            rw [← AlgEquiv.mul_apply, ← map_mul, mul_inv_cancel, map_one, AlgEquiv.one_apply]
          rw [hcancel]
          ring
        rw [hinv]
        exact neg_mem (hg (ρ g⁻¹ a)) }
  have hg₀H : g₀ ∈ H := fun a ↦ Ideal.subset_span ⟨a, rfl⟩
  have hle : Subgroup.zpowers g₀ ≤ H := Subgroup.zpowers_le.2 hg₀H
  exact fixedPointIdeal_le_iff.2 fun g a ↦ hle (hg₀ g) a

end Cyclic

section FinitePresentation

/-- When `Γ` is finite and `A` is a finite-type `R`-algebra, `fixedPointIdeal ρ` is finitely
generated as an ideal of `A`. -/
theorem fg_fixedPointIdeal {R A Γ : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]
    [Monoid Γ] [Finite Γ] [Algebra.FiniteType R A] (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) :
    (fixedPointIdeal ρ).FG := by
  classical
  cases nonempty_fintype Γ
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := Algebra.FiniteType.out (R := R) (A := A)
  let t : Finset A := (Finset.univ ×ˢ s).image fun p ↦ ρ p.1 p.2 - p.2
  refine ⟨t, le_antisymm ?_ (fixedPointIdeal_le_iff.2 fun γ a ↦ ?_)⟩
  · rw [Ideal.span_le]
    rintro _ hp
    obtain ⟨⟨γ, a⟩, -, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 hp
    exact sub_mem_fixedPointIdeal ρ γ a
  · -- For fixed `γ`, the elements whose `γ`-displacement lies in `Ideal.span t` form an
    -- `R`-subalgebra containing the generating set `s`.
    let S : Subalgebra R A :=
      { carrier := {x : A | ρ γ x - x ∈ Ideal.span (t : Set A)}
        mul_mem' {x y} hx hy := by
          have hleib : ρ γ (x * y) - x * y = (ρ γ x - x) * ρ γ y + x * (ρ γ y - y) := by
            rw [map_mul]
            ring
          rw [Set.mem_ofPred, hleib]
          exact add_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ hx) (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hy)
        one_mem' := by simp
        add_mem' {x y} hx hy := by
          rw [Set.mem_ofPred, map_add, add_sub_add_comm]
          exact add_mem hx hy
        zero_mem' := by simp
        algebraMap_mem' r := by simp }
    have hsS : Algebra.adjoin R (s : Set A) ≤ S :=
      Algebra.adjoin_le fun x hx ↦ Ideal.subset_span <|
        Finset.mem_coe.2 (Finset.mem_image.2 ⟨(γ, x), Finset.mem_product.2 ⟨Finset.mem_univ γ, hx⟩,
          rfl⟩)
    rw [hs] at hsS
    exact hsS Algebra.mem_top

/-- When `Γ` is finite and `A` is finitely presented over `R`, the fixed-point quotient
`A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ` is finitely presented over `R`. -/
theorem finitePresentation_quotient_fixedPointIdeal {R A Γ : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing A]
    [Algebra R A] [Monoid Γ] [Finite Γ] [Algebra.FinitePresentation R A]
    (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) :
    Algebra.FinitePresentation R (A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ) := by
  refine Algebra.FinitePresentation.of_surjective (f := Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R (fixedPointIdeal ρ))
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective ?_
  rw [AlgHom.toRingHom_eq_coe, Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_ker]
  exact fg_fixedPointIdeal ρ

end FinitePresentation

section Smooth

private theorem finite_or_subsingleton_of_isUnit_natCard {R Γ : Type*} [Semiring R]
    (hΓ : IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R)) : Finite Γ ∨ Subsingleton R := by
  rcases finite_or_infinite Γ with hfin | hinf
  · exact .inl hfin
  · rw [Nat.card_eq_zero_of_infinite, Nat.cast_zero] at hΓ
    obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hΓ
    exact .inr (subsingleton_of_zero_eq_one (by rw [← hu, ← u.mul_inv, hu, zero_mul]))

private def reynoldsLiftAlgHom {R A B Γ : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]
    [CommRing B] [Algebra R B] [Group Γ] [Fintype Γ] (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A))
    (c : R) (hcB : algebraMap R B c * (Fintype.card Γ : B) = 1)
    {I : Ideal B} (hI : I ^ 2 = ⊥) (f₀ : A →ₐ[R] B)
    (hδ : ∀ (γ : Γ) (a : A), f₀ (ρ γ a) - f₀ a ∈ I) : A →ₐ[R] B :=
  let D : A → B := fun a ↦ c • ∑ γ : Γ, (f₀ (ρ γ a) - f₀ a)
  have hD (a : A) : D a ∈ I := by
    dsimp only [D]
    rw [Algebra.smul_def]
    exact I.mul_mem_left _ (sum_mem fun γ _ ↦ hδ γ a)
  have hI_mul {x y : B} (hx : x ∈ I) (hy : y ∈ I) : x * y = 0 :=
    Ideal.mem_bot.1 (hI ▸ sq I ▸ Ideal.mul_mem_mul hx hy)
  have havg (a : A) : c • ∑ γ : Γ, f₀ (ρ γ a) = f₀ a + D a := by
    have hsplit (γ : Γ) : f₀ (ρ γ a) = f₀ a + (f₀ (ρ γ a) - f₀ a) := (add_sub_cancel _ _).symm
    dsimp only [D]
    conv_lhs => arg 2; arg 2; ext γ; rw [hsplit γ]
    rw [Finset.sum_add_distrib, smul_add, Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, nsmul_eq_mul,
      Algebra.smul_def c, ← mul_assoc, hcB, one_mul]
  { toFun a := c • ∑ γ : Γ, f₀ (ρ γ a)
    map_one' := by rw [havg 1]; simp [D]
    map_mul' a b := by
      rw [havg (a * b), havg a, havg b]
      have hδ_mul (γ : Γ) : f₀ (ρ γ (a * b)) - f₀ (a * b) =
          f₀ a * (f₀ (ρ γ b) - f₀ b) + (f₀ (ρ γ a) - f₀ a) * f₀ b := by
        rw [map_mul, map_mul, map_mul]
        linear_combination hI_mul (hδ γ a) (hδ γ b)
      have hD_mul : D (a * b) = f₀ a * D b + D a * f₀ b := by
        simp only [D, hδ_mul, Finset.sum_add_distrib, ← Finset.mul_sum, ← Finset.sum_mul,
          smul_add, mul_smul_comm, smul_mul_assoc]
      linear_combination map_mul f₀ a b + hD_mul - hI_mul (hD a) (hD b)
    map_zero' := by simp
    map_add' a b := by simp only [map_add, Finset.sum_add_distrib, smul_add]
    commutes' r := by rw [havg (algebraMap R A r)]; simp [D] }

/-- **Invariant lifting across a square-zero extension.** Let `Γ` be a group with
`IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R)` acting on `A`, `I` a square-zero ideal of a commutative `R`-algebra `B`,
and `g : A →ₐ[R] B ⧸ I` a `Γ`-invariant homomorphism. If `g` admits an `R`-algebra lift
`f₀ : A →ₐ[R] B`, then `g` admits a `Γ`-invariant `R`-algebra lift `f : A →ₐ[R] B`. -/
theorem exists_invariant_lift_of_sq_eq_bot {R A Γ : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [CommRing A]
    [Algebra R A] [Group Γ] (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) (hΓ : IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R))
    {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra R B] {I : Ideal B} (hI : I ^ 2 = ⊥)
    {g : A →ₐ[R] B ⧸ I} (hg : ∀ γ : Γ, g.comp (ρ γ : A →ₐ[R] A) = g)
    (f₀ : A →ₐ[R] B) (hf₀ : (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R I).comp f₀ = g) :
    ∃ f : A →ₐ[R] B, (∀ γ : Γ, f.comp (ρ γ : A →ₐ[R] A) = f) ∧
      (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R I).comp f = g := by
  rcases finite_or_subsingleton_of_isUnit_natCard hΓ with hfin | hsub
  · classical
    cases nonempty_fintype Γ
    obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := (Nat.card_eq_fintype_card (α := Γ) ▸ hΓ : IsUnit (Fintype.card Γ : R))
    let c : R := ↑u⁻¹
    have hcB : algebraMap R B c * (Fintype.card Γ : B) = 1 := by
      rw [← map_natCast (algebraMap R B), ← map_mul, mul_comm, ← hu, u.mul_inv, map_one]
    have hfg (a : A) : Ideal.Quotient.mk I (f₀ a) = g a := DFunLike.congr_fun hf₀ a
    have hδ (γ : Γ) (a : A) : f₀ (ρ γ a) - f₀ a ∈ I := by
      have hgi : g (ρ γ a) = g a := DFunLike.congr_fun (hg γ) a
      rw [← Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, map_sub, hfg, hfg, hgi, sub_self]
    refine ⟨reynoldsLiftAlgHom ρ c hcB hI f₀ hδ,
      fun σ ↦ AlgHom.ext fun a ↦ ?_, AlgHom.ext fun a ↦ ?_⟩
    · simp only [reynoldsLiftAlgHom, AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgEquiv.coe_toAlgHom, AlgHom.coe_mk,
        RingHom.coe_mk, MonoidHom.coe_mk, OneHom.coe_mk]
      refine congrArg (c • ·) ?_
      have hstep (γ : Γ) : f₀ (ρ γ (ρ σ a)) = f₀ (ρ (Equiv.mulRight σ γ) a) := by
        simp only [Equiv.coe_mulRight, map_mul, AlgEquiv.mul_apply]
      simp_rw [hstep]
      exact Equiv.sum_comp (Equiv.mulRight σ) (fun γ : Γ ↦ f₀ (ρ γ a))
    · have hg_eq (γ : Γ) : g (ρ γ a) = g a := DFunLike.congr_fun (hg γ) a
      simp only [reynoldsLiftAlgHom, AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgHom.coe_mk, RingHom.coe_mk,
        MonoidHom.coe_mk, OneHom.coe_mk, map_smul, map_sum, Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk, hfg, hg_eq,
        Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ]
      rw [← Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul R, smul_smul, ← hu, u.inv_mul, one_smul]
  · have : Subsingleton B := Module.subsingleton R B
    have : Subsingleton (B ⧸ I) := Module.subsingleton R (B ⧸ I)
    exact ⟨f₀, fun _ ↦ Subsingleton.elim _ _, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩

section CommRingBase

variable {R A Γ : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] [Group Γ]

/-- **Edixhoven's tame fixed-point formal smoothness theorem.** Let `Γ` be a group whose order
`Nat.card Γ` is invertible in `R`, acting on a formally smooth `R`-algebra `A` by `R`-algebra
automorphisms `ρ`. Then the fixed-point quotient `A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ` is formally smooth over
`R` (Edixhoven, Prop. 3.4, pp. 294–295). -/
theorem formallySmooth_quotient_fixedPointIdeal [Algebra.FormallySmooth R A]
    (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) (hΓ : IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R)) :
    Algebra.FormallySmooth R (A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ) := by
  refine Algebra.FormallySmooth.of_comp_surjective fun B _ _ I hI gbar ↦ ?_
  let g := fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv ρ (B ⧸ I) gbar
  obtain ⟨f₀, hf₀⟩ := Algebra.FormallySmooth.comp_surjective R A I hI g.1
  obtain ⟨f, hf_inv, hf_lift⟩ := exists_invariant_lift_of_sq_eq_bot ρ hΓ hI g.2 f₀ hf₀
  refine ⟨(fixedPointQuotientAlgHomEquiv ρ B).symm ⟨f, hf_inv⟩, ?_⟩
  apply Ideal.Quotient.algHom_ext
  ext a
  exact DFunLike.congr_fun hf_lift a

/-- **Edixhoven's tame fixed-point smoothness theorem.** Let `Γ` be a group whose order
`Nat.card Γ` is invertible in `R`, acting on a smooth `R`-algebra `A` by `R`-algebra automorphisms
`ρ`. Then the fixed-point quotient `A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ` is smooth over `R`
(Edixhoven, Props. 3.1 and 3.4, pp. 293–295). -/
theorem smooth_quotient_fixedPointIdeal [Algebra.Smooth R A]
    (ρ : Γ →* (A ≃ₐ[R] A)) (hΓ : IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R)) :
    Algebra.Smooth R (A ⧸ fixedPointIdeal ρ) where
  formallySmooth := formallySmooth_quotient_fixedPointIdeal ρ hΓ
  finitePresentation := by
    rcases finite_or_subsingleton_of_isUnit_natCard hΓ with hfin | hsub
    · exact finitePresentation_quotient_fixedPointIdeal ρ
    · have : Subsingleton A := Module.subsingleton R A
      refine Algebra.FinitePresentation.of_surjective
        (f := Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R (fixedPointIdeal ρ)) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective ⟨∅, ?_⟩
      ext x
      simp [Subsingleton.elim x 0]

end CommRingBase

end Smooth

section ReynoldsRetract

variable {R B Γ : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [CommRing B] [Algebra R B] [Group Γ]

private theorem reynoldsFinsum_mem_range (ρ : Γ →* (B ≃ₐ[R] B)) (hΓ : IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R))
    (hfix : ∀ b : B, (∀ γ : Γ, ρ γ b = b) → b ∈ Set.range (algebraMap R B)) (b : B) :
    ∃ r : R, algebraMap R B r = (↑hΓ.unit⁻¹ : R) • ∑ᶠ γ : Γ, ρ γ b := by
  rcases finite_or_subsingleton_of_isUnit_natCard hΓ with hfin | hsub
  · cases nonempty_fintype Γ
    exact hfix _ fun σ ↦ by
      rw [finsum_eq_sum_of_fintype, map_smul, map_sum]
      refine congrArg ((↑hΓ.unit⁻¹ : R) • ·) ?_
      have hstep (γ : Γ) : ρ σ (ρ γ b) = ρ (Equiv.mulLeft σ γ) b := by
        simp only [Equiv.coe_mulLeft, map_mul, AlgEquiv.mul_apply]
      simp_rw [hstep]
      exact Equiv.sum_comp (Equiv.mulLeft σ) (fun γ : Γ ↦ ρ γ b)
  · have : Subsingleton B := Module.subsingleton R B
    exact ⟨0, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩

/-- If `Γ` is a group with `IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R)`, `algebraMap R B` is injective, and every
`Γ`-fixed element of `B` lies in `Set.range (algebraMap R B)`, Reynolds averaging yields an
`R`-linear retraction `B →ₗ[R] R` of `algebraMap R B`. -/
def linearRetractOfIsUnitCard (ρ : Γ →* (B ≃ₐ[R] B)) (hΓ : IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R))
    (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap R B))
    (hfix : ∀ b : B, (∀ γ : Γ, ρ γ b = b) → b ∈ Set.range (algebraMap R B)) : B →ₗ[R] R where
  toFun b := (reynoldsFinsum_mem_range ρ hΓ hfix b).choose
  map_add' b₁ b₂ := hinj <| by
    rw [map_add, (reynoldsFinsum_mem_range ρ hΓ hfix (b₁ + b₂)).choose_spec,
      (reynoldsFinsum_mem_range ρ hΓ hfix b₁).choose_spec,
      (reynoldsFinsum_mem_range ρ hΓ hfix b₂).choose_spec]
    rcases finite_or_subsingleton_of_isUnit_natCard hΓ with hfin | hsub
    · cases nonempty_fintype Γ
      simp only [finsum_eq_sum_of_fintype, map_add, Finset.sum_add_distrib, smul_add]
    · have : Subsingleton B := Module.subsingleton R B
      exact Subsingleton.elim _ _
  map_smul' r b := hinj <| by
    rw [RingHom.id_apply, smul_eq_mul, map_mul, ← Algebra.smul_def,
      (reynoldsFinsum_mem_range ρ hΓ hfix (r • b)).choose_spec,
      (reynoldsFinsum_mem_range ρ hΓ hfix b).choose_spec]
    rcases finite_or_subsingleton_of_isUnit_natCard hΓ with hfin | hsub
    · cases nonempty_fintype Γ
      simp only [finsum_eq_sum_of_fintype, map_smul, ← Finset.smul_sum,
        smul_comm (↑hΓ.unit⁻¹ : R) r]
    · have : Subsingleton B := Module.subsingleton R B
      exact Subsingleton.elim _ _

/-- Applying `algebraMap R B` to `linearRetractOfIsUnitCard ρ hΓ hinj hfix b` computes the
Reynolds average `(Nat.card Γ : R)⁻¹ • ∑ᶠ γ, ρ γ b`. -/
theorem algebraMap_linearRetractOfIsUnitCard (ρ : Γ →* (B ≃ₐ[R] B)) (hΓ : IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R))
    (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap R B))
    (hfix : ∀ b : B, (∀ γ : Γ, ρ γ b = b) → b ∈ Set.range (algebraMap R B)) (b : B) :
    algebraMap R B (linearRetractOfIsUnitCard ρ hΓ hinj hfix b) =
      (↑hΓ.unit⁻¹ : R) • ∑ᶠ γ : Γ, ρ γ b :=
  (reynoldsFinsum_mem_range ρ hΓ hfix b).choose_spec

/-- `linearRetractOfIsUnitCard` retracts `algebraMap R B`. -/
@[simp]
theorem linearRetractOfIsUnitCard_algebraMap (ρ : Γ →* (B ≃ₐ[R] B)) (hΓ : IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R))
    (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap R B))
    (hfix : ∀ b : B, (∀ γ : Γ, ρ γ b = b) → b ∈ Set.range (algebraMap R B)) (r : R) :
    linearRetractOfIsUnitCard ρ hΓ hinj hfix (algebraMap R B r) = r := by
  rcases finite_or_subsingleton_of_isUnit_natCard hΓ with hfin | hsub
  · cases nonempty_fintype Γ
    have hcu : (Fintype.card Γ : R) * ↑hΓ.unit⁻¹ = 1 :=
      Nat.card_eq_fintype_card (α := Γ) ▸ IsUnit.mul_val_inv hΓ
    apply hinj
    rw [algebraMap_linearRetractOfIsUnitCard, finsum_eq_sum_of_fintype]
    simp only [AlgEquiv.commutes, Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ, ← Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul R]
    rw [smul_smul, mul_comm (↑hΓ.unit⁻¹ : R), hcu, one_smul]
  · exact Subsingleton.elim _ _

/-- Every `Γ`-fixed element of `B ⊗[R] T` lies in the image of `T` and is recovered by applying
`linearRetractOfIsUnitCard` to the `B`-tensor factor. -/
theorem includeRight_lid_rTensor_linearRetractOfIsUnitCard_of_fixed (ρ : Γ →* (B ≃ₐ[R] B))
    (hΓ : IsUnit (Nat.card Γ : R)) (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap R B))
    (hfix : ∀ b : B, (∀ γ : Γ, ρ γ b = b) → b ∈ Set.range (algebraMap R B))
    (T : Type*) [Semiring T] [Algebra R T] (z : B ⊗[R] T)
    (hz : ∀ γ : Γ, Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor T (ρ γ : B →ₐ[R] B) z = z) :
    Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.lid R T
        (LinearMap.rTensor T (linearRetractOfIsUnitCard ρ hΓ hinj hfix) z)) = z := by
  rcases finite_or_subsingleton_of_isUnit_natCard hΓ with hfin | hsub
  · cases nonempty_fintype Γ
    have hcu : (Fintype.card Γ : R) * ↑hΓ.unit⁻¹ = 1 :=
      Nat.card_eq_fintype_card (α := Γ) ▸ IsUnit.mul_val_inv hΓ
    let π := linearRetractOfIsUnitCard ρ hΓ hinj hfix
    let L₁ : B ⊗[R] T →ₗ[R] B ⊗[R] T :=
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : T →ₐ[R] B ⊗[R] T).toLinearMap.comp
        ((Algebra.TensorProduct.lid R T).toLinearMap.comp (LinearMap.rTensor T π))
    let L₂ : B ⊗[R] T →ₗ[R] B ⊗[R] T :=
      (↑hΓ.unit⁻¹ : R) • ∑ γ : Γ, (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor T (ρ γ : B →ₐ[R] B)).toLinearMap
    have hL : L₁ = L₂ := by
      apply TensorProduct.ext'
      intro b t
      simp only [L₁, L₂, LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.rTensor_tmul, AlgEquiv.toLinearMap_apply,
        Algebra.TensorProduct.lid_tmul, AlgHom.toLinearMap_apply,
        Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, LinearMap.sum_apply,
        Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor, Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul, AlgHom.id_apply,
        AlgEquiv.coe_toAlgHom]
      rw [← TensorProduct.smul_tmul, Algebra.smul_def, mul_one,
        algebraMap_linearRetractOfIsUnitCard, finsum_eq_sum_of_fintype, ← TensorProduct.smul_tmul',
        TensorProduct.sum_tmul]
    have hzL := DFunLike.congr_fun hL z
    simp only [L₁, L₂, LinearMap.comp_apply, AlgHom.toLinearMap_apply, AlgEquiv.toLinearMap_apply,
      LinearMap.smul_apply, LinearMap.sum_apply, hz, Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ,
      ← Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul R] at hzL
    rwa [smul_smul, mul_comm (↑hΓ.unit⁻¹ : R), hcu, one_smul] at hzL
  · have : Subsingleton (B ⊗[R] T) := Module.subsingleton R _
    exact Subsingleton.elim _ _

end ReynoldsRetract

section TensorSwap

variable (R A : Type*) [CommSemiring R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]

/-- The action of `Multiplicative (ZMod 2)` on `A ⊗[R] A` whose generator `ofAdd 1` swaps the two
tensor factors via `Algebra.TensorProduct.comm R A A`. -/
def tensorSwapAction : Multiplicative (ZMod 2) →* ((A ⊗[R] A) ≃ₐ[R] (A ⊗[R] A)) :=
  (TauCeti.zmodMonoidHomEquiv 2 ((A ⊗[R] A) ≃ₐ[R] (A ⊗[R] A))).symm
    ⟨Algebra.TensorProduct.comm R A A, AlgEquiv.coe_toAlgHom_injective <|
      Algebra.TensorProduct.ext' fun _ _ ↦ rfl⟩

/-- The generator `ofAdd 1` of `Multiplicative (ZMod 2)` acts on `A ⊗[R] A` by
`Algebra.TensorProduct.comm R A A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem tensorSwapAction_ofAdd_one :
    tensorSwapAction R A (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1) = Algebra.TensorProduct.comm R A A :=
  TauCeti.zmodMonoidHomEquiv_symm_apply_ofAdd_one _

/-- Over any commutative semiring `R`, the displacement ideal of `tensorSwapAction R A` on
`A ⊗[R] A` is the kernel of multiplication `Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul' R : A ⊗[R] A →ₐ[R] A`. -/
theorem fixedPointIdeal_tensorSwapAction :
    fixedPointIdeal (tensorSwapAction R A) =
      RingHom.ker (Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul' R (S := A)) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ fun z hz ↦ ?_
  · rw [fixedPointIdeal_eq_span_of_mem_zpowers _ (.ofAdd 1) Multiplicative.mem_zpowers_ofAdd_one,
      tensorSwapAction_ofAdd_one, Ideal.span_le, Set.range_subset_iff]
    intro x
    have hcomm : (Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul' R (S := A)).comp
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.comm R A A : A ⊗[R] A →ₐ[R] A ⊗[R] A) =
        Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul' R (S := A) := by
      apply Algebra.TensorProduct.ext'
      intro a b
      simpa only [AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgEquiv.coe_toAlgHom, Algebra.TensorProduct.comm_tmul,
        Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul'_apply_tmul] using mul_comm b a
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, RingHom.mem_ker, map_sub, sub_eq_zero]
    exact DFunLike.congr_fun hcomm x
  · -- Modulo `fixedPointIdeal (tensorSwapAction R A)`, `1 ⊗ₜ b ≡ b ⊗ₜ 1`, so every tensor `z` is
    -- congruent to `lmul' z ⊗ₜ 1`.
    let J := fixedPointIdeal (tensorSwapAction R A)
    have hmk_eq : (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R J).comp
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft.comp (Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul' R (S := A))) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R J := by
      apply Algebra.TensorProduct.ext'
      intro a b
      simp only [AlgHom.comp_apply, Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul'_apply_tmul,
        Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft_apply, Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk]
      have hcomm : Ideal.Quotient.mk J ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] b) =
          Ideal.Quotient.mk J (b ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)) := by
        have hmem := sub_mem_fixedPointIdeal (tensorSwapAction R A) (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)
          (b ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A))
        rw [tensorSwapAction_ofAdd_one, Algebra.TensorProduct.comm_tmul] at hmem
        exact Ideal.Quotient.eq.2 hmem
      have hprod : (a * b) ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A) = (a ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)) * (b ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)) := by
        rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, mul_one]
      have hprod' : a ⊗ₜ[R] b = (a ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)) * ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] b) := by
        rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, mul_one, one_mul]
      rw [hprod, hprod', map_mul, map_mul, hcomm]
    have hmz := DFunLike.congr_fun hmk_eq z
    simp only [AlgHom.comp_apply, Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk] at hmz
    have hzero : Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul' R (S := A) z = 0 := RingHom.mem_ker.1 hz
    rw [hzero, map_zero, map_zero] at hmz
    exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.1 hmz.symm

/-- The fixed-point quotient of `A ⊗[R] A` under `tensorSwapAction R A` is canonically isomorphic
to `A` via multiplication `a ⊗ₜ b ↦ a * b` and the left inclusion `a ↦ a ⊗ₜ 1`. -/
def quotientFixedPointIdealTensorSwapAlgEquiv :
    ((A ⊗[R] A) ⧸ fixedPointIdeal (tensorSwapAction R A)) ≃ₐ[R] A :=
  (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq R (fixedPointIdeal_tensorSwapAction R A)).trans
    (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfRightInverse
      (f := Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul' R (S := A))
      (g := (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft : A →ₐ[R] A ⊗[R] A))
      fun a ↦ by simp)

/-- `quotientFixedPointIdealTensorSwapAlgEquiv` sends the class of `a ⊗ₜ b` to `a * b`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientFixedPointIdealTensorSwapAlgEquiv_mk_tmul (a b : A) :
    quotientFixedPointIdealTensorSwapAlgEquiv R A
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (fixedPointIdeal (tensorSwapAction R A)) (a ⊗ₜ[R] b)) = a * b := by
  rw [quotientFixedPointIdealTensorSwapAlgEquiv, AlgEquiv.trans_apply,
    Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq_mk]
  rfl

end TensorSwap

end TauCeti.Algebra
